/* Growth is calculated as the difference between the starting point and ending point */
/* Usually the Ending Point is the Current Period and the greatest value. */
/* The starting point is the smallest value for the comparison */

/* Example: In current year 2024 we sell 3.102.292 units of PCs */
/* In 2020 we only sold 2.834.292 units. 
What is the growth of units sold? 

1) Find Begining year: 2020 (2.834.292)
2) Find Ending year: 2024 (3.102.292)
3) Find the difference between Beginning Year and Ending Year: 
    (Ending Year - Beginning Year)
    (3.102.292 - 2.834.292 = 268.000)

Growth = 
CALCULATE(
    [Sales] - [Sales Last Period]
)

4) Find the growth in percent between Beginning Year and Ending Year: 
    (Ending Year - Beginning Year / Beginning Year)
    (3.102.292 - 2.834.292 / 2.834.292 = 0.0945 * 100 = 9,45%)

Use this method everytime to get the numbers correct!

Growth Pct. = 
CALCULATE(
    DIVIDE(
        [Sales] - [Sales Last Period],
        [Sales Last Period]
    )
)